            <ArticleTitle>Combined off-pump coronary artery bypass grafting and aorto-bicarotid bypass.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>58-60</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 63-year-old man with severe coronary artery disease and occlusion of aortic arch branches presented with dizziness, syncope and unstable angina. He underwent a combined surgical procedure of aorto-bicarotid bypass and off-pump myocardial revascularization. The operation was successful and he had no complications during 11 months of follow-up.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
